<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/alerts">Operations Alerts</a> (under Management in the menu) is one list of the problems
        Lanyard has noticed at your venue (kiosks, automation rules, missed clock-ins, overdue training and expiring staff
        documents), so you don't have to piece them together from separate emails and
        notifications. Admins and Managers can open it.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Who sees what">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Managers</strong> see the alerts for the location they signed in to.</li>
            <li><strong>Admins</strong> see every location in the company, plus company-wide alerts, such as a kiosk or
                rule that isn't set to a location. Admins also get a <strong>Location</strong> filter and a link to the
                kiosk or automation page.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="The page">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Open</strong> lists alerts that haven't been resolved yet, most severe first. The count next to
                the heading says how many are open, acknowledged and critical.</li>
            <li><strong>History (90 days)</strong> lists alerts that were resolved, by a person or automatically, in the
                last 90 days. Press <strong>Show more</strong> for older ones.</li>
            <li><strong>Type</strong> and <strong>Severity</strong> narrow the list.</li>
            <li>Each alert shows its severity as a word and an icon (<strong>Critical</strong>, <strong>Warning</strong> or
                <strong>Info</strong>), what it's about, when it was raised and, if it keeps happening, how many times
                it has been seen.</li>
            <li>New alerts appear without reloading, and screen readers announce them. The number beside
                <strong>Operations Alerts</strong> in the menu is how many are still waiting to be acknowledged.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpNote>
        Alerts can be switched off for a company under Manage &gt; Companies &amp; Locations (<strong>Operations
        alerts</strong>). While it's off, no new alerts are recorded. Kiosk notifications are still sent.
    </HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
